\noindent Here we use the fact that $\displaystyle \sum_{k\geq 0}\binom{n-k}{k}=F_{n}$.

\label{prop:B_calc}
We have that $\bar b_1=1$ and if $n\geq 2$, then $\bar b_n=2^{n-1}-1$.  It follows that
\[\sum_{n\geq 1}\bar b_n\, x^n=\frac{x-2x^2+2x^3}{(1-2x)(1-x)}.\]

The fact that $\bar b_1=1$ is clear.  Let $\mathcal{D}=\{B_1,\ldots,B_k\}$ be a strongly connected staircase diagram on $[n]$ and let $\alpha_i:=|B_i|$.  If $\mathcal{D}$ avoids $Q_B$, then it consists of alternating $2$-chains with non-empty overlaps between blocks. Define $\beta_i=|B_i\cap B_{i+1}|$ for $i<k$ with $\beta_k=0$ and $\gamma_i=\alpha_i-(\beta_i+\beta_{i-1})$ (here we set $\beta_0=0$). If $k>1$, then the map 
$$\mathcal{D}\rightarrow (\gamma_1,\beta_1,\gamma_2,\beta_2\ldots,\gamma_k)$$
